-- title:
--   Origin chart maps from solutions of the dehomogenised Weierstrass cubic
-- statement:
--   Let $T$ be a commutative ring and $W$ a Weierstrass cubic over $T$, with coefficients $a_1,a_2,a_3,a_4,a_6$; let $B$ be a commutative $T$-algebra and $x,v\in B$ two elements satisfying the dehomogenised cubic relation
--   $$v + a_1 x v + a_3 v^2 = x^3 + a_2 x^2 v + a_4 x v^2 + a_6 v^3,$$
--   the coefficients being read in $B$ through the structure map. Here the projective model of $W$ is the quotient $T[X_0,X_1,X_2]/(W_{\hom})$ of the polynomial ring by the ideal generated by the homogeneous Weierstrass cubic, graded by the images of the homogeneous submodules of the standard grading, and `OriginChartRing W` is the homogeneous localisation of this graded ring away from the image $\bar X_1$ of the second coordinate, i.e. the degree-zero part of the localisation at the powers of $\bar X_1$; inside it, `xOverY W` and `zOverY W` are the fractions $\bar X_0/\bar X_1$ and $\bar X_2/\bar X_1$. The assertion is that there exists a ring homomorphism $\chi$ from `OriginChartRing W` to $B$ which is compatible with the scalars, in the sense that for every $t\in T$ the image under $\chi$ of the canonical image in the homogeneous localisation of the degree-zero element $t$ equals the image of $t$ in $B$, and which satisfies $\chi(\bar X_0/\bar X_1)=x$ and $\chi(\bar X_2/\bar X_1)=v$. Only existence is asserted; no uniqueness claim is made.
--
--   This is the existence half of the presentation of the origin chart $D_+(Y)$ of the projective Weierstrass model by the two affine coordinates $X/Y$ and $Z/Y$ subject to the dehomogenised cubic: a solution of that cubic in any $T$-algebra is realised by a scalar-compatible ring map from the chart. It is the tool used to produce maps out of the origin chart, for instance the formal chart with values in a power series ring, and is cited in the construction of the origin parameter and of quotient presentations of the chart ring.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_WeierstrassCurve_DrinfeldGlobal_exists_ringHom_originChartRing_eq.lean

